WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Part 3. You will hear Holly, a student on an events management course, talking to her tutor about her work placement.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:16.000
First, you have some time to look at questions 21 to 24.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:52.000
Now listen carefully and answer questions 21 to 24.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:58.000
Hello Dr Green. I'm here to talk to you about my work placement.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Oh yes, it's Holly isn't it?

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.000
Yes.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:04.000
So, which work placement have you chosen?

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:08.000
I decided to go for the Orion Stadium placement.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:15.000
The event I'll be managing is one where I'm helping to set up a sports competition for primary school children.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:21.000
Yep, that's always a popular placement, even though it can be tougher than you think working with children.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:30.000
I know, but it's the fresh air that attracts me. Organising something indoors doesn't have the same appeal, even though it might be fun.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:36.000
OK, so obviously safety is going to be one of your key concerns for this event.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:43.000
Yes, I've already thought about that. I'll need to make sure none of the equipment's damaged.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:48.000
Ah, well, you'll be working with schools, so the equipment will be their responsibility.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:52.000
However, the grounds and what goes on there will be yours.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Oh, I see. That'll include keeping everyone within the boundary once they're in their kit and on the field?

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:07.000
Exactly. You'll need to inspect areas like changing rooms as well, for anything someone can trip over.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:10.000
But your main priority will be not to lose anyone.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:14.000
Right. I'll need staff to help with that.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.000
And don't forget about the spectators.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:22.000
I was thinking that many of them will be parents who could help run the event.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:28.000
I wouldn't rely on that. They'll be more interested in filming their children than volunteering.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:32.000
I'll need to make sure they don't interfere with events doing that.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:40.000
And that's not always easy, especially when a proud parent's trying to get a snap of their child and you want them to move elsewhere.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:44.000
OK. What about the scheduling?

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:51.000
With sporting events, there are all sorts of things that can alter the timetable, like rain for instance,

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:55.000
though so far we've always been lucky with that.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:03:00.000
Yeah, and I was thinking about what to do if someone got hurt as well.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:04.000
I know that last year that caused a terrible delay.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:06.000
You have to be prepared for such things.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:13.000
Oh, what if a match ends in a draw? Do you let the teams keep going until someone wins?

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:17.000
That'll be up to you. And again, you need to plan for it.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.000
Right.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:29.000
Before you hear the rest of the discussion, you have some time to look at questions 25 to 30.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:41.000
Now listen and answer questions 25 to 30.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:14.000
Now, the aim of your work placement is to give you the opportunity to develop the skills that an events manager needs.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:17.000
So let's talk about those a bit.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:21.000
Well, I think my communication skills are pretty good.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:26.000
I can talk on the phone to people and book venues and that kind of thing.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:30.000
Good. Just remember it isn't only about what you say.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:35.000
If you meet someone face to face and want to persuade them to be a sponsor, for example…

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:38.000
Oh, I'll dress up for that. Sure.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:43.000
Good. Let's go on to think about your organisational skills.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:49.000
You're working in a very people-based industry and that means things won't always go to plan.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:53.000
I guess it's being prepared to make changes that matters.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:05:00.000
That's right. You may have to make an on-the-spot change to a timetable because of a problem you hadn't anticipated.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:02.000
Just do it. OK.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:05.000
How's your time management these days?

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:12.000
I'm working on it. I'm certainly better when I have a deadline, which is why this work suits me.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:16.000
Yes, but it's how you respond as that deadline approaches.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:20.000
I know I've got to look calm even if I'm in a panic.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:24.000
Just think to yourself, no one must know I'm under pressure.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:28.000
Yeah, even though I'm multitasking like crazy.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:32.000
Another skill that events managers need is creativity.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:36.000
Often your client has what we call the big picture idea,

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:42.000
but it's up to the events manager to think of all the fine points that go to making it work.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:48.000
Right. So I need to listen carefully to that idea and then fill in all the gaps.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:55.000
That's right. And you'll have a team working under you, so another key skill is leadership.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:06:01.000
Your team may have lots of ideas too, but you've got to make the ultimate choices.

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:05.000
Do we have refreshments inside or out, for example?

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:08.000
Isn't it better to be democratic?

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:12.000
It's a nice idea, but you have the ultimate responsibility.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:17.000
So believe in what you think best. Be prepared to say,

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:21.000
yes, that's a good idea, but it won't work here.

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:26.000
I see what you mean. What about the networking side of things?

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:29.000
I know it's an area that a lot of students worry about,

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:33.000
because we don't have much experience to offer others.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:39.000
But even without it, you can still be an interesting person with useful ideas,

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:42.000
and the more people you impress, the better.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:45.000
I guess that will help me when I apply for a real job.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:51.000
Exactly. Think ahead, remember what your ambitions are and keep them in mind.

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:52.000
Definitely.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:16.000
Thank you.

